 "id": "S25",
 "text": "After Kansas City, the industry tightened how connection designs and shop drawings are reviewed. Today, a change like that two-rod detail is supposed to trigger a fresh calculation, not just a stamp. The Hyatt Regency is now taught in engineering ethics classes across the United States. Not because the physics is complicated. It's one rod, two nuts, and a load that doubled. It's taught because the number was always there to be checked.",
